# UPSTREAM-BASELINE.sha256
#
# Per-file SHA-256 baseline for every upstream byte this package carries:
# GNU MPFR 4.2.2. GMP is a separate package dependency.
#
# This record is the machine-checkable statement of that claim. It is derived
# from the pinned upstream sources named below, never from this working tree,
# and it is verified from the repository root by
#
#     ./check-upstream-baseline.sh
#
# which checks that every carried upstream byte still hashes to the pin, that
# every divergence from the pin is one this file records, that the counts below
# are the counts in this file, and that nothing else is carried. CI runs the
# same script from the `licence-and-provenance` job of
# `.github/workflows/verify.yml`.
#
# The body of this file is plain `sha256sum` format, so
#
#     sha256sum -c UPSTREAM-BASELINE.sha256
#
# is also a valid check, and the narrower one: it verifies the carried bytes
# and nothing else. It does not verify that the path set is complete, that a
# divergence is recorded rather than tolerated, or that the counts are true.
# The script is what makes the record complete rather than merely accurate.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------ pin 1 ---
# project        GNU MPFR
# canonical SCM  https://gitlab.inria.fr/mpfr/mpfr.git
# tag            4.2.2
# tag object     736ef3903ce50fc592268f69b6895c73da6adfb4
# commit         eaa57b856d814af32f97d5e5eb129fb986235323
# tree           c769e6ab3b026c5ff2d017832d3cbc67a8eb5c8e
# commit date    2025-03-20 10:15:52 +0100
# commit subject ChangeLog update with tools/update-changelog
# paths          654 blobs; no symlink, no gitlink, no submodule
#
# These two values are also stated in `UPSTREAM.md`, and the checker fails if
# the two documents stop agreeing:
#
# pin-echo: eaa57b856d814af32f97d5e5eb129fb986235323 (MPFR commit; also in UPSTREAM.md)
# pin-echo: 736ef3903ce50fc592268f69b6895c73da6adfb4 (MPFR annotated tag object; also in UPSTREAM.md)
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------- derivation ---
# MPFR is pinned by a commit, so its digests come from git at that commit:
#
#     git init mpfr-pin && cd mpfr-pin
#     git remote add origin https://gitlab.inria.fr/mpfr/mpfr.git
#     git fetch --depth 1 origin refs/tags/4.2.2:refs/tags/4.2.2
#     git rev-parse refs/tags/4.2.2            # 736ef3903ce50fc592268f69b6895c73da6adfb4
#     git rev-parse refs/tags/4.2.2^commit     # eaa57b856d814af32f97d5e5eb129fb986235323
#     git rev-parse refs/tags/4.2.2^tree       # c769e6ab3b026c5ff2d017832d3cbc67a8eb5c8e
#     git ls-tree -r refs/tags/4.2.2           # 654 entries
#     git archive --format=tar refs/tags/4.2.2 | tar -x -C mpfr-git
#     (cd mpfr-git && find . -type f -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum)
#
# `git archive` writes each blob's exact content, so these are digests of the
# upstream bytes and not of a checkout of them. `git ls-tree -r` reports 654
# entries on that commit and every mode is 100644 or 100755, so no upstream
# path is a symlink a `find -type f` walk would silently leave out.
#
# ------------------------------------------------ cross-check, not the source --
# `UPSTREAM.md` names an archive fallback for MPFR. It was fetched as well and
# it is the source of no digest here, because it is not the imported tree:
#
#     https://www.mpfr.org/mpfr-current/mpfr-4.2.2.tar.xz, 1505596 bytes,
#     sha256 b67ba0383ef7e8a8563734e2e889ef5ec3c3b898a01d00fa0a6869ad81c6ce01
#
# It is a `make dist` product: 572 files against the 654 tracked at the pin. It
# carries generated autotools output this tree does not have (`configure`,
# `aclocal.m4`, `Makefile.in`, `install-sh`, `ltmain.sh`, `test-driver`,
# `m4/libtool.m4` and the rest) and omits repository files this tree does have
# (`tests/data/*`, `doc/algorithms.tex`, `doc/algorithms.bib`, `.gitignore`,
# `.mailmap`, `codespell.exclude`, `codespell.ignore`, `other/*`, the two
# `libtool-tcc-*.patch` files and others). The Git tag is the pin, because the
# Git tag is what `UPSTREAM.md` records and what this tree was imported from.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------- counts ---
# count: carried upstream paths in this baseline = 654
# count: GNU MPFR 4.2.2 at eaa57b856d81 = 654
# count: byte-identical to the pin = 653
# count: recorded divergences from the pin = 1
# count: fork-owned paths carried alongside (excluded below) = 40
# area: doc = 18
# area: examples = 7
# area: m4 = 2
# area: other = 2
# area: root = 23
# area: src = 291
# area: tests = 258
# area: tools = 48
# area: tune = 5
#
# What each area is, in the words of the record:
#
#   src/     291   libmpfr's 261 C sources and 27 headers, plus `src/Makefile.am`
#                 and the `src/mparam_h.in` template the build copies to
#                 `mparam.h`. The arch subdirectories (`amd`, `arm`, `x86`,
#                 `x86_64`, `mips`, `powerpc64`, `sparc64`, `generic`) are
#                 upstream's and are carried unused.
#   tests/   258   upstream's own test programs -- `tversion.c`, `tvalist.c`,
#                 `tyn.c`, `RRTest.c`, `turandom.c` and the rest -- plus the 42
#                 files of `tests/data/`.
#   tools/    48   upstream's own maintenance tooling: `mpfrlint`,
#                 `gitlog-to-changelog`, `get_patches.sh`, the `ck-*` checks,
#                 `check_mparam.c`, `bench/`, `metaMPFR/`, `mbench/`.
#   doc/      18   the manual sources (`mpfr.texi`, `texinfo.tex`, `fdl.texi`),
#                 the algorithms papers (`algorithms.tex`, `algorithms.bib`),
#                 `FAQ.html` and the maintenance scripts.
#   examples/  7, tune/ 5, m4/ 2, other/ 2   upstream's example programs, tuning
#                 programs, libtool m4 and the two standalone programs under
#                 `other/`.
#   root      23   upstream's 23 tracked root files: the licence texts `COPYING`
#                 and `COPYING.LESSER`; the build files `Makefile.am`,
#                 `configure.ac`, `acinclude.m4`, `autogen.sh`, `version-ext.sh`,
#                 `mpfr.pc.in`, `PATCHES`, `libtool-tcc-rpath.patch`,
#                 `libtool-tcc-wl.patch`; and the documentation records `README`,
#                 `INSTALL`, `NEWS`, `TODO`, `AUTHORS`, `BUGS`, `ChangeLog`,
#                 `VERSION`, `codespell.exclude`, `codespell.ignore`,
#                 `.mailmap`, `.gitignore`.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------ what is left out --
# Excluded from the baseline, each with the reason it is not an omission:
#
#   * This fork's own 40 files, declared below. They are listed rather
#     than assumed, so that a path which is neither upstream nor declared is a
#     gate failure instead of an unnoticed gap: an unrecorded file under
#     `src/` is a native file nothing is checking.
#   * Upstream's `README` is in the baseline under its upstream name, with the
#     digest `UPSTREAM.md` records for it. The fork's byte-for-byte copy of that
#     file is `README.upstream.md`, which is fork-owned because it is the fork's
#     file; the checker holds its digest equal to the `README` entry, so two
#     files with one content and two different digests is a gate failure.
#   * `.gitignore` is an upstream file the fork extends additively. It is a
#     recorded divergence rather than a manifest entry, because a manifest
#     entry means "byte-identical to the pin" and this file is not.
#   * Build outputs (`.zig-cache/`, `zig-out/`, `zig-pkg/`) and the `.git` directory are not
#     carried bytes; the coverage scan skips them by directory name.
#   * File modes are not bytes and are not part of a SHA-256 baseline. The pin
#     records MPFR's modes, and no carried file is executable that upstream did
#     not mark executable.
#
# ------------------------------------------------- recorded divergence (1) ---
# divergence: .gitignore upstream=e363fac26f837cd1c3357f9b2ce08325c5e8adde9a9dc496bcde61f86be8837f carried=6e7047860c580040aa6575d305484e5ef132872c1c74722cec31d70337171fe8 upstream_bytes=440 carried_bytes=1371 policy=upstream-bytes-are-a-prefix-of-carried
#
# `.gitignore` is the only upstream-tracked file this fork has ever changed, and
# `CHANGELOG.md` section 5 and `UPSTREAM.md` both record that. The carried file
# is upstream's 440 bytes unchanged, followed by 19 appended lines:
# ignores for `/.zig-cache/`, `/zig-out/`, `/result`, `/.devenv*` and `/.direnv*`,
# each with its reasoning in comments. Nothing above that block was touched,
# which the `licence-and-provenance` job's own `git diff --numstat` step checks
# independently of this record. The checker cannot verify the prefix rule
# offline, because it holds digests and not upstream bytes; what it does verify
# is that the carried file is exactly the 1371-byte file this record
# describes, so any further edit to it fails the gate.
#
# `UPSTREAM.md` says the file differs "by ten added lines". The carried file has
# 19 appended lines and is 1371 bytes against upstream's
# 440. The prose carries the stale number; the file is the one that
# was measured.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------ verbatim copy ---
# verbatim-copy: README.upstream.md = README
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------- fork-owned files ---
# Every carried path that is not upstream, so that coverage is total in both
# directions. A `fork-owned-prefix:` line covers a whole directory of fork work
# and needs no edit when a file is added inside it; a `fork-owned-file:` line
# is one exact path and does have to exist.
#
# fork-owned-file: .envrc
# fork-owned-file: CHANGELOG.md
# fork-owned-file: FORK-LICENSE.md
# fork-owned-file: FORK-NOTES.md
# fork-owned-file: NOTICE.md
# fork-owned-file: README.md
# fork-owned-file: README.upstream.md
# fork-owned-file: README.zig.md
# fork-owned-file: UPSTREAM-BASELINE.sha256
# fork-owned-file: UPSTREAM.md
# fork-owned-file: build.zig
# fork-owned-file: build.zig.zon
# fork-owned-file: check-upstream-baseline.sh
# fork-owned-file: devenv.nix
# fork-owned-file: devenv.yaml
# fork-owned-file: flake.lock
# fork-owned-file: flake.nix
# fork-owned-file: package.nix
# fork-owned-file: root.zig
# fork-owned-prefix: .github/
# fork-owned-prefix: consumer/
# fork-owned-prefix: fork/
# fork-owned-prefix: runtime/
# fork-owned-prefix: zig/
#
